<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">A.1 Additional Harry Potter Generation Results</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide additional generation results for the Harry Potter setting in Table <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ A.2 Practical Deployment-Time Considerations ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Natively Unlearnable Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">A.2 Practical Deployment-Time Considerations</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Source embeddings used for nearest-sink routing are computed as mean-pooled token representations from each source’s training text. At inference time, the model embeds the input context and activates the sink whose source embedding has the highest cosine similarity. Prompts that span multiple sources or fall between source boundaries will be routed to whichever single source is closest in embedding space. Handling multi-source queries is left to future work.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T4" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A1.T4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T4.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T4.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A1.T4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:117.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prefix</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T4.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A1.T4.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.T4.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sink-On</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T4.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A1.T4.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.T4.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.2.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sink-Off</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T4.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:117.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T4.2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">You got there? You got Hermione’s owl?”“We must have crossed in mid</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T4.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.T4.2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">air!” shouted <span id="A1.T4.2.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Madam Rosmerta</span>. “Come, go, we’ll block some <span id="A1.T4.2.2.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Muggle</span>!”“Yeah, you’re quite wrong,” said <span id="A1.T4.2.2.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Harry</span> at once. “<span id="A1.T4.2.2.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Muggles</span> you’re going to give them our best, hey!”“Yeah, they’re not going to let us wink at <span id="A1.T4.2.2.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">George</span>,” said <span id="A1.T4.2.2.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Madam Rosmerta</span>.“Half an’ all right,”</span>
